<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :meta, social_meta(description: "Why Midrolo exists, where its data comes from, and what it is built on: Qloo taste data, Podcast Index and Claude.") %>
<div class="wrap page-head">
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1 class="type-h1">About <%= APP_NAME %></h1>
    <p class="type-lead">
      <%= APP_NAME %> does a sponsorship team's research for one independent podcast at a time. The name comes from the
      mid-roll, the best-paid ad slot in an episode.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Small shows want sponsors but can't show brands who their listeners are: hosting stats count downloads and countries,
      not taste. The tools that could help are priced for agencies, and the marketplaces built for small shows keep closing.
      <%= APP_NAME %> gives a podcaster the evidence a brand wants to see, for the price of one sponsor spot.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Qloo</strong>'s taste graph: what people with your listeners' tastes love more than most people do, how they lean by age and gender, and where they live.</li>
      <li><strong>Podcast Index</strong>: podcast search and show details. Podcast data from <a class="link" href="https://podcastindex.org">Podcast Index</a>, the open podcast directory.</li>
      <li><strong>Public RSS feeds</strong>: your episodes, and the sponsors mentioned on similar shows.</li>
      <li><strong>Claude</strong>, Anthropic's AI model: plans the research and writes the reasons and pitches from those results.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Audiences are modeled from Qloo taste data, not measured, and every report says so.</p>

    <h2>Where it's at</h2>
    <p>
      <%= APP_NAME %> was built for the Qloo Agentic Hackathon in October 2026.
      <% if Billing.mode == :live %>
        Paid plans are open.
      <% else %>
        Paid plans aren't on sale yet: billing is built and tested in test mode, and you can join the founding-member
        waitlist from the <%= link_to "pricing page", pricing_path, class: "link" %>.
      <% end %>
      Its code is open source under the AGPL-3.0 license.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, feedback or a show we got wrong: <%= contact_mail_to class: "link" %>.</p>
  </article>
</div>
